# Moss turf 0: a round, springy cushion of hair-cap moss about 0.45 m tall and 0.5 m across, a dome of olive-green moss with a
# younger, brighter crown, nine sporophyte stalks fanning up and out of it, each topped by a plump rust-brown spore capsule.
# The moss counterpart of grass-turf0, with the same footprint and height; few chunky shapes so it stays light to scatter.
# Few, chunky shapes rather than a bristle of fine ones, so it stays light enough to scatter by the hundreds.
format 1

# Detail as the grass and flowers have it: the fine stalks and thin stems are small next to the model's size
Detail detail=0.45
    Intersection
        Union
            Material material=moss_soil
                Translate translation=(0, 0, 0)
